{
  "dom_id": "step-1035",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Removing Jump Discontinuities From Rational Functions",
  "problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the function defined below. Find the values of $k$ for which $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14196844/assets/ad328ab7996bbdacac0284ecf282c610bebc3ba7959ddb25dcc78123a5d91384.svg)",
  "worked_solution": "From the definition of $f(x)$, the left-sided limit of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x-12}{{x}^{2}-4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{(x-2)(x+6)}{(x-2)(x+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x+6)}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{x+6}{x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+6}{2+2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}{2}^{kx} \\\\  & ={2}^{2k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also note that $f(2) = 2^{2k}.$\n\nSo, for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) \\\\ {2}^{2k} & =2 \\\\ {2}^{2k} & ={2}^{1} \\\\ 2k & =1 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\dfrac12$ removes the discontinuity at $x=2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-1035\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"1035\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"268\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-1035\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-5\">Removing Jump Discontinuities From Rational Functions</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"1035\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                   